WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:12.605
Messier 39 or M39, also known as NGC 7092, is an open cluster of stars in the constellation of Cygnus, sometimes referred to as the Pyramid Cluster.

00:13.135 --> 00:19.386
It is positioned two degrees south of the star Pi Cygni and around 9° east-northeast of Deneb.

00:19.916 --> 00:28.686
The cluster was discovered by Guillaume Le Gentil in 1749, then Charles Messier added it to his catalogue in 1764.

00:29.396 --> 00:37.803
When observed in a small telescope at low power the cluster shows around two dozen members but is best observed with binoculars.
